    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n57302" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κη-ώδης</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ες</span>,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κη</span>- cogn. with <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κήϊα, καίω; -ώδης</span> with <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄδωδα</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>smelling as
				of incense, fragrant</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μιν κηώδεϊ δέξατο κόλπῳ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					6.483
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κηώδεα φύετο πάντα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.P.
					941
				</span></i>
			; cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κεώδης</span>.</div>
